Falsifies `credential_contract::proofs::no_reply_word_but_match_ever_authenticates`.

The defect: the reply-code range loses its upper bound. Codes are a small run starting at `OK`,
so "at least OK" looks like the whole test, and every word a live service sends still decodes
correctly.

Expected to fail: the harness's second claim, `None => assert!(!(OK..=MAX_CODE).contains(&r0))`,
for any word above `MAX_CODE`: an arbitrary kernel error word now decodes as a reply code. The
first assertion survives, because `is_authenticated` still asks for `MATCH` exactly, which is why
this harness states the discrimination as well as the authentication.

